        <body>
            <div xml:id="d660">

                <pb facs="1060" n="964" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg964"/>

                <head>No. 658.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Sickles to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation in Spain</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 28, 1873</date>.
                        (Received December 23.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 887.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to forward herewith copies
                    of communications recently exchanged between the Count Maffei, the Italian
                    charge d’affaires in Madrid, and myself, respecting the authorization granted to
                    the former by the cabinet of Rome to take charge of the effects of this legation
                    and of American interests in event of my departure from Spain.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer><signed>D. E. SICKLES.</signed></closer>





